#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068915 :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/correct {:answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482713} :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482720}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f49ac21a-2d62-566e-a42d-88814c785a3f" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{48}}9 \\sin{\\left(24 x \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=24 x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=24\\,\\Longrightarrow\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{24}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{48}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{48}}9 \\sin{\\left(24 x \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= {\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}9\\sin(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{24}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sin(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= - \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{8}\\big|_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\ &= 0-\\left(- \\frac{3}{8}\\right) \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
